The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**`. That
path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group (the app targets list
`Sources` + `TeslaSync/{widget-primitives,dashboard-widgets,feature-views,misc-surfaces,
shared-surfaces}` — there is no `TeslaSync/Features`). The repo's real, compiled canonical
admin-page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**` — where every sibling P7 admin page
(AuditLog, ApiPlayground, DiskForecast, SchemaDrift, FleetTelemetryCoverage, RbacMatrix,
Users, …) ships and which `Sources` already lists as a project.yml source path
(createIntermediateGroups). The page therefore ships at `apps/apple/Sources/Features/Admin/**`,
the faithful equivalent of the prompt's `Features/Admin`. This is the identical reconciliation
the AuditLog / DiskForecast / SchemaDrift logs recorded; it is the only deviation from the
literal prompt path.

ROUTE HOSTING: the web route is the admin sub-path `/admin/feedback`. Following the sibling
AuditLog/Users pattern, a dedicated `.feedbackQueue` AppRoute case is added (pathSegment
`feedback`, System group, icon `exclamationmark.bubble.fill`), `AppRouteParser` aliases
`/admin/feedback` → `.feedbackQueue`, and `FeedbackQueueRouteRegistration` hosts
`FeedbackQueuePage` on it, chained into `\.routeHosts` in TeslaSyncApp.swift. So the page is
reachable via the System-group sidebar entry and any `/admin/feedback` deep link. (Navigation
registration is an allowed file per the prompt.)

