DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI FeedbackQueuePage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure
@Observable state holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) exposing the list state
(loading/empty/error/success) over an injectable FeedbackDataSource seam whose value types mirror
the web FeedbackEntry / FeedbackListResponse / FeedbackUpdateInput 1:1 (production binds the KMP
admin-feedback endpoints through the seam). The page reproduces the web chrome (PageContainer
title) and the single GlassPanel: the status/category filter menus + Refresh + the
"bridge not configured" note, and the paginated entries table with an adaptive layout (columnar
Grid on macOS/iPad, per-row cards on iPhone) covering all seven web columns plus the expandable
detail (report body, app-version/user-agent/submitter/masked-email metadata, recent-errors +
console-tail disclosures, and the triage action row — change status / save GitHub issue URL /
bridge-gated Forward). It binds the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (TSGlassPanel, TSSelect,
TSButton, TSTextField, TSMaskedValue, TSBadge, TSUserCell, TSTableSkeleton, TSEmptyState,
TSQueryError — no hand-rolled chrome). Every visible string resolves from Localizable.xcstrings
with the web key names (38 keys, already present under the catalog's translation.* namespace);
date/JSON formatting is ported from the web and unit-tested. Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated
Swift-6 strict-concurrency type-checks (macOS 0/0 + iOS 0/0, exercising the compact branches) and
an executed model harness (33 assertions passed). The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to a
pre-existing, out-of-scope compile error in the generated TeslaSync/shared-surfaces
(Input.Previews.swift), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

